WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.769
PAUL: 68 meters.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.237
DAVE: Okay.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.605
PAUL: This is the
easy part you know.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.140
MINDY: Ha, exactly.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.510
NARRATOR: Racing for a
million dollar prize,

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.380
Team North America,
three co-workers
from Denver,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.749
have just seven hours
to complete a complex,

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.817
three-stage climb.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.587
The first pitch
against the lower face,

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.856
will allow them to
get their bearings.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.492
Pitch two is a brutal
mid-air vertical ascent

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.327
to an overhang.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.797
And finally pitch three, a
battle against exhaustion up a

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:35.168
crevasse to the end of
day waypoint, Tree Ledge,

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.537
where they'll be
spending the night.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.372
MINDY: Yeah.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.374
PAUL: How are you feeling?
A little more at ease?

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:45.845
MINDY: A little bit.
Till you start going up.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:51.184
I'm not good at ledges,
I, I get a little, little
scared on the ledges.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:55.188
DAVE: Part of me wonders,
should she go first?

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.792
You're probably gonna
be the fastest, I don't
feel that matters.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:00:59.926
PAUL: A bit like a sandwich.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.661
DAVE: Yeah, let's do a
sandwich, let's do a sandwich.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.096
Paul go for it.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.231
MINDY: I think I wanna
see how this goes.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.235
PAUL: It, it feels
a little awkward.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.570
MINDY: It's a little awkward?

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.743
PAUL: Oh, oh my.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.778
DAVE: Nice.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.680
Get in that rhythm.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.783
NARRATOR: The wall ascent
uses clamps and foot stirrups

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.587
attached to a fixed rope,
which tighten then relax as

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.857
climbers shift their weight
and move upward in small steps,

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.258
like a ladder.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.561
It's a technique
known as "jumaring".

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.165
PAUL: My foot, ah!

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.501
MINDY: You're killing it Paul!

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.574
DAVE: This is a
full-on suffer fest.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.144
PAUL: I was a
gymnast for my entire childhood,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.879
leading up and
through college.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:59.519
I'm a strong, motivated
and gritty competitor.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.354
PAUL: Oh.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.189
Nice.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.858
We made it.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.794
DAVE: Well done Paul!

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:11.631
You may not hear me,
but I'm clapping loudly.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:15.401
Oh thanks, why don't you send
down some debris on us.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.104
Careful, debris.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.506
NARRATOR: A
passionate climber,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:24.477
Paul Montague Junior
crushes the first pitch
in just 15 minutes,

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.146
building a massive
lead for the team.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.350
PAUL: A big motivator for
me just being out here,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.352
is to show you know,
representation.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.220
Climbing you know,
big mountaineering.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.389
You don't really see a
lot of people of color.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.491
And there should be more.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.426
If some little, you know,

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.429
kid out there is flipping
through the TV and,

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.697
I'm on the
side of a mountain.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.534
They go wow, like
he, he looks like me,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.304
or maybe I didn't know people
of color did that or whatever.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.239
I think that's,
you know, inspiring.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.474
DAVE: Take your time Paul.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.742
Captioned by Cotter Media Group.

